  "interpretation": [
    "All first drafts scored 6/17 under the frozen checker; every repaired draft passed 17/17. Do not change those scores retrospectively.",
    "The checker requires a retained-path fragment in refusal diagnostics. The common task does not explicitly request that string content, and the frozen specification records path and reason separately. Treat this as an extra diagnostic requirement, not proof of data-loss behavior.",
    "For 86 failed case results, removable returned an error and the next path-text assertion failed. The test then stopped before later content-integrity assertions. This supports classification of the observed failure; it does not establish a new safety-only acceptance score.",
    "Only controls 1 and 8 approved removal for the unknown ignored parent containing private/target/notes.bin. The failing assertion occurs before remove is called, so these are unsafe approvals, not observed deletions.",
    "The repeated diagnostic failures share a generic refusal message and are not independent defects. All eight runs required repair feedback that exposed this diagnostic expectation.",
    "The known development case supports advancement under the registered acceptance gate. Its 12.36% median cost reduction is below the 20% cost-win threshold; three of four treatment runs were cheaper. Do not use development results as held-out evidence.",
    "The measured primary wall-time reduction includes unusually slow control setup. Tool counts and secondary timings are descriptive; neither establishes that the brief caused the entire difference."
  ]
